# Task 3 #

## Collecting Network Information ##

I opened up PowerShell on the Windows host and got the list of all adapters using the Get-NetAdapter function. I was able to identify a VirtualBox Host-Only Ethernet Adapter and use Get-NetIPAddress -InterfaceAlias VirtualBox Host-Only to check the IPv4 address. The default host address for this lab is 192.168.56.1. I also ran the Get-NetRoute -DestinationPrefix "192.168.56.1." command to look for 192.168.56.1/24.



I then logged into OpenWRT via PuTTY and executed ip addr to see if I could see any guest interfaces. I has recorded eth0, eth1 and br-mng with their ip addresses. I then ran the command ip route to see the routing table. The default route is crucial as it determines to OpenWRT where to route internet traffic when it is not being sent through some of its other interfaces. It is usually the NAT interface.



Device	Interface	IP Address	VirtualBox Adapter Type	Purpose
